@bank rank:junior
// Writer 4, batch 3. Everyday chatter for the junior crew on Deck 4: the bunks, mornings, the washrooms, the
// laundry, the junior common room, weekends. Not about work. Neutral in voice; specific by conditions. A line
// naming someone carries !who: so that person never says it. Bubbles: 60 characters.

== smalltalk
// ---- the bunks ----
? place:bunk_1|bunk_2|bunk_3|bunk_4|bunk_5|bunk_6|bunk_7|bunk_8
- Whose sock is this? It's been here a week.   #funny
- Top bunk's warmer. Bottom bunk's nearer. Fair.
- Someone's snoring. It's not me. It's never me.   #funny
- Five minutes. I'm just resting my eyes.
- Who's got the good pillow? I want the good pillow.
- Shoes off the ladder, please. Thank you.
- Somebody tidied. Who tidied? I can't find anything.   #funny
- I've got a letter to finish. Shh. Thinking.
- Lights out soon. I'm reading one more page.
- My bunk smells of oranges. I don't know why.   #funny
- Don't sit on my bunk, it's made. It's made!   #funny
- Is that the vent or someone humming?
- Who's left a biscuit tin open? Is it the chef's?
- I'll do my bunk tomorrow. It knows that.   #funny
? place:bunk_1|bunk_2|bunk_3|bunk_4|bunk_5|bunk_6|bunk_7|bunk_8 time:night
- Who's still awake? Me. Just me. Night.
- Somebody's talking in their sleep again.   #funny
- Can't sleep. Counting rivets on the ceiling.
- Night, everyone. Night. No, really, night.   #funny
? place:bunk_1|bunk_2|bunk_3|bunk_4|bunk_5|bunk_6|bunk_7|bunk_8 time:morning
- Is it morning? It feels like the middle of the night.
- Who took my other boot? This is the left one. Both are left.   #funny
- Up, up. Breakfast's not going to eat itself.
- I dreamt about cake. It wasn't a good cake.   #funny
? place:bunk_1|bunk_2|bunk_3|bunk_4|bunk_5|bunk_6|bunk_7|bunk_8 act:off
- Rest day. I'm not getting out of this bunk till ten.
- Rest day. I tidied my shelf. That's enough for today.
- Rest day. Reading under the blanket like I'm nine.   #funny
? place:bunk_8
- Shh. Day sleepers. Tiptoe, please.
- Night shift's room. Quiet, even at noon.

// ---- mornings and the washrooms ----
? place:port_washroom|starboard_washroom
- Who's singing? Lovely. Keep going. Mostly.   #funny
- Has anyone seen my toothbrush? The blue one.
- The mirror's all steamed. I look like a ghost.   #funny
- Two minutes in the shower. I'm counting. Go.
- The dawn chorus is in good voice today.   #funny
- Who left a towel on the floor? Again?
? place:port_washroom|starboard_washroom time:night
- Hot water's gone. It's character-building time.   #funny
- Cold shower. I'm awake now. Very awake.   #funny
? place:port_washroom|starboard_washroom time:morning
- Queue for the sinks. There's always a queue.
- Hot water's lovely before seven. Remember that.
? time:morning act:wash
- Shower, teeth, breakfast. In that order.
- Somebody's singing the quiz song. Badly.   #funny
? time:morning
- Is breakfast still on? Run!
- Has anyone got a spare comb? Thanks.
- Big yawn. Sorry. Long night.
- Who's for porridge? I'm for porridge.
- Good morning, Deck 4. Mostly good.   #funny

// ---- the laundry ----
? place:laundry
- Whose is this jumper? It's very orange.   #funny
- Everything I own is in that machine.
- I've lost a sock. Again. The machine eats them.   #funny
- I like the folding. Don't laugh.
- Warm laundry. Best smell on the ship.   #warm
- Somebody's washed a red shirt with the whites.   #funny
- Whose turn on the dryer? I'll wait.
- I fold my shirts in three. My mum folds in four.
- Somebody left a note in a pocket. "Buy biscuits."   #funny
? place:laundry act:off
- Rest day laundry. Living the dream.   #funny
- I'll sit here till it's done. It's warm.

// ---- the junior common room ----
? place:commons
- Who's got the Tiles board? Fancy a game?
- Comics wall's got a new one. Have you seen it?
- That window. All those stars. Never gets old.
- Somebody's left a jigsaw. Half a sky.
- Cushion fort. Don't ask. It's for later.   #funny
- Tea for anyone? I'm making a pot.
- Who moved the good chair? It was by the window.
- I'm going to read till dinner. Nobody talk.   #funny
- There's a blanket on the sofa. Is it anyone's?
- Somebody's drawn me on the comics wall. As a cloud.   #funny
- Is the record player working? Somebody hum.   #funny
- Swap you a biscuit for the window seat.
? place:commons !who:rina
- Who's playing Rina at Tiles? Brave.   #funny
- Rina's on forty-something wins. Don't look at the book.   #funny
- Has anyone beaten Rina yet? No. Course not.   #funny
? place:commons time:evening
- Film on later. Somebody bring a blanket.
- Evening in the common room. Best room on the ship.   #warm
- Tiles, tea, nobody needing anything. Lovely.
? place:commons time:night
- Last cup of tea, then bed. Promise.
- The stars are brighter from here at night.
? place:commons act:off
- Rest day. Common room. Jigsaw. Done.
- I've been on this sofa since breakfast. It's fine.   #funny

// ---- weekends and rest days ----
? act:off weekday:sat
- Saturday. No alarm. I woke up at six anyway.   #funny
- Saturday lie-in. Then a long breakfast.
- It's Saturday. I'm wearing my good socks.   #funny
- Saturday. Laundry, letters, nap. Perfect.
? act:off weekday:sun
- Sunday. Bread smells from the galley. Lovely.
- Swap meet's on. I'm taking my old book.
- Sunday call home. Then a long sit.
- Sunday's a slow day. Good.
? act:off
- Rest day. I'm doing absolutely nothing. Watch me.   #funny
- Rest day plan: tea, book, tea.
- I slept till nine. I feel like a new person.
- Rest day. I'm writing home. It's a long one.
- Rest day. I fixed my bunk curtain. Proud.   #funny
- Went to the garden. Sat by the pond. An hour went.
- Rest day. Gym, then a nap. Balanced.   #funny
- I'm going to the store. I don't need anything.   #funny
- Rest day! I've no idea what day it is.   #funny
- Spent the morning on the jigsaw. Still half a sky.
? act:off time:evening
- Back to it tomorrow. Today was nice, though.
- Rest day done. I didn't waste it. Mostly.   #funny

// ---- Deck 4 at large ----
? deck:4
- Lift's slow today. Take the long way.
- Somebody's baking. Smell that?
- The corridor smells of toast. Good sign.
- Is the music room free? Somebody's on the piano.
- Somebody's left a tiny portrait on my bunk.   #funny
- There's a new Gerald on the windowsill. Small one.
- Hot water's good till ten. Then it's character.   #funny
? deck:4 !who:tran-chloe
- Chloe says lights out at ten. Chloe means it.   #funny
? deck:4 !who:torres-zeke
- Torres has knitted another scarf. It's long.   #funny
? deck:4 !who:tomas
- Tomas is at the stern window again. Leave him be.
? deck:4 time:evening
- Who's for a film? Bring a cushion.
- Somebody's playing guitar badly. Lovely.   #funny
? deck:4 time:night
- Quiet in the corridor. Just the vents.
- Somebody's late back. Tiptoe!   #funny

// ---- the seasons on Deck 4 ----
? deck:4 season:sowing
- Everyone's got a seedling on the windowsill.
- My seedling's taller than yours. Just.   #funny
? deck:4 season:greening
- The garden smell's got all the way up here.
? deck:4 season:harvest
- Somebody's left a pumpkin in the common room.   #funny
? deck:4 season:lanterns
- Lanterns in every bunk window. It's lovely.
- My lantern's wonky. It's still a lantern.   #funny

// ---- the traditions ----
? deck:4 trad:quiz
- Quiz tonight. Our team's going to win. Probably not.   #funny
? deck:4 trad:film
- Film night. I'm bringing my blanket from the bunk.
? deck:4 trad:jam
- Music night. Is anyone borrowing my guitar? No? Good.
? deck:4 trad:observatory-night
- Observatory night. Wrap up warm. It isn't cold. Still.
? deck:4 trad:market
- Swap meet today. I'm swapping my old jumper.

// ---- more of the everyday ----
? deck:4 birthday:me
- It's my birthday. Somebody's hidden a cake. I can smell it.   #warm
- Birthday! I got a card from the whole bunk.   #warm
? deck:4 act:off !who:tomas
- Tomas showed me his star map. He knows every one.
? place:musicroom
- Somebody's put the good record on. Shh.
- Is the piano free? I only know one tune.   #funny
- I'm on the waiting list for the good records. Still.   #funny
- The guitar book's missing a page. The hard page.   #funny
? place:musicroom time:evening
- Music room at night. Best place to sit and think.
? deck:4 act:meal
- Are you going up to dinner? Wait for me.
- I've been thinking about pudding since lunch.   #funny
? deck:4
- Has anyone seen my mug? It's got a chip. That one.
- Who's got a needle and thread? Button trouble.
- I wrote my mum six pages. She'll write back one.   #funny
- Somebody's put a plant in the corridor. Nice.
- I've borrowed a book from the common room. Third time.
- The stern windows are best before bed.
- Somebody's leaving notes on the comics wall. Nice ones.
- I love it when the whole bunk's asleep and it's quiet.   #warm
- Biscuits from the galley! On the common room table!
- Who's going to the gym? I'll come and watch.   #funny
? deck:4 time:morning
- Odd sock day. Nobody'll notice. Everyone will.   #funny
- I made my bunk. Look. Corners and everything.
? deck:4 time:evening
- Letters tonight. Then bed. Then letters in my head.   #funny
- Long day. I'm going to sit by the stern window.
- Anyone for cocoa? I've got a tin.
? deck:4 act:off weekday:sat|sun
- Weekend. The whole deck's in socks.   #funny
- Weekend breakfast. Nobody's rushing. Lovely.

== rumour
? deck:4
- Heard it in the washroom queue. So it's true.   #funny
- Bunk news: something's going on. Nice something.
- Common room says it's true. The common room knows.
- Somebody said it over Tiles. Here it is.
- Laundry gossip's the best gossip. Listen.   #funny
